mance\n\nIn fiscal year 2026, Autodesk's revenue was $7.21 billion, an increase of 17.53% compared to the previous year's $6.13 billion. Earnings were $1.12 billion, an increase of 1.08%.\n\n## Analyst Summary\n\nAccording to 36 analysts, the average rating for ADSK stock is \"Buy.\" The 12-month stock price target is $307.54, which is an increase of 21.94% from the latest price.\n\nPrice Target $307.54 (21.94% upside) Analyst Consensus: Buy\n\n### Autodesk price target lowered to $338 from $369 at Piper Sandler\n\nPiper Sandler lowered the firm’s price target on Autodesk (ADSK) to $338 from $369 and keeps an Overweight rating on the shares. The firm says Q7 was another consistent result…\n\n1 month ago - TheFly\n\n### Autodesk price target raised to $283 from $277 at Guggenheim\n\nGuggenheim analyst Tamjid Chowdhury raised the firm’s price target on Autodesk (ADSK) to $283 from $277 and keeps a Buy rating on the shares. Autodesk reported “a clean quarter, exceeding…\n\n1 month ago - TheFly\n\n### Why Autodesk Stock Is Dropping After Earnings Beat\n\nThe software maker reported a mixed outlook for the third quarter and full year, with profit projections that fall short of expectations, and revenue projections that beat Wall Street's estimates.\n\n1 month ago - Barrons\n\n### Autodesk forecasts quarterly profit below Wall Street estimates, shares dip\n\nAutodesk forecast third-quarter adjusted profit below expectations on Thursday, sending its shares ​down more than 5% in extended trading, as investors worry ‌over the potential disruption from AI too...\n\n1 month ago - Reuters\n\n### Autodesk Earnings Call Transcript: Q2 2027\n\nRevenue and EPS surpassed guidance, leading to raised full-year outlooks and inclusion of MaintainX. Construction and Fusion segments showed strong growth, while guidance reflects improved business momentum and prudent risk management. MaintainX integration and evolving AI strategy are key focus areas.\n\n### Autodesk Slides: Q2 2027\n\nAutodesk has posted slides in relation to its Q2 2027 quarterly earnings report, which was published on August 27, 2026.\n\n### Autodesk Earnings release: Q2 2027\n\nAutodesk released its Q2 2027 earnings on August 27, 2026, summarizing the period's financial results.","title":"Autodesk (ADSK) Stock Price & Overview","url":"https://stockanalysis.com/stocks/adsk/"},{"author":null,"id":"https://stockanalysis.com/stocks/adsk/statistics/","image":"https://stockanalysis.com/stockanalysis-1200x630.png","text":"Autodesk (ADSK) Statistics & Valuation\n\n252.20 -2.75 (-1.08%) At close: Oct 23, 2026, 4:00 PM EDT\n\n251.39 -0.81 (-0.32%) After-hours: Oct 23, 2026, 7:55 PM EDT\n\n## Total Valuation\n\nAutodesk has a market cap or net worth of $52.71 billion. The enterprise value is $52.06 billion.\n\n| Market Cap | 52.71B |\n| --- | --- |\n| Enterprise Value | 52.06B |\n\n## Important Dates\n\nThe next estimated earnings date is Tuesday, November 24, 2026, after market close.\n\n| Earnings Date | Nov 24, 2026 |\n| --- | --- |\n| Ex-Dividend Date | n/a |\n\n## Share Statistics\n\nAutodesk has 209.01 million shares outstanding. The number of shares has decreased by -1.62% in one year.\n\n| Current Share Class | 209.01M |\n| --- | --- |\n| Shares Outstanding | 209.01M |\n| Shares Change (YoY) | -1.62% |\n| Shares Change (QoQ) | -0.47% |\n| Owned by Insiders (%) | 0.15% |\n| Owned by Institutions (%) | 100.01% |\n| Float | 208.44M |\n\n## Valuation Ratios\n\nThe trailing PE ratio is 32.68 and the forward PE ratio is 19.40. Autodesk's PEG ratio is 1.20.\n\n| PE Ratio | 32.68 |\n| --- | --- |\n| Forward PE | 19.40 |\n| PS Ratio | 6.77 |\n| Forward PS | 6.01 |\n| PB Ratio | 15.58 |\n| P/TBV Ratio | n/a |\n| P/FCF Ratio | 18.57 |\n| P/OCF Ratio | 18.20 |\n| PEG Ratio | 1.20 |\n\n## Enterprise Valuation\n\nThe stock's EV/EBITDA ratio is 22.77, with an EV/FCF ratio of 18.34.\n\n| EV / Earnings | 31.70 |\n| --- | --- |\n| EV / Sales | 6.68 |\n| EV / EBITDA | 22.77 |\n| EV / EBIT | 23.79 |\n| 