ops computational, AI-driven software, hardware, and silicon intellectual property products and solutions. The company offers functional verification services, such as Jasper, a formal verification platform; Xcelium, a parallel logic simulation platform; Verisium, a generative AI solution; Palladium, an enterprise emulation platform; and Protium, a prototyping platform for chip verification, as well as digital IC design and sign off products, including Innovus platform; and custom IC design and simulation produ... [Read more]\n\nIndustry Software - Application\n\nSector Technology\n\nIPO Date Jun 10, 1987\n\nEmployees 13,800\n\nStock Exchange Nasdaq\n\nTicker Symbol CDNS\n\nWebsite https://www.cadence.com\n\n## Financial Performance\n\nIn 2025, Cadence Design Systems's revenue was $5.30 billion, an increase of 14.12% compared to the previous year's $4.64 billion. Earnings were $1.11 billion, an increase of 5.06%.\n\n## Analyst Summary\n\nAccording to 25 analysts, the average rating for CDNS stock is \"Strong Buy.\" The 12-month stock price target is $406.24, which is an increase of 28.36% from the latest price.\n\nPrice Target $406.24 (28.36% upside) Analyst Consensus: Strong Buy\n\nSAN JOSE, Calif.--(BUSINESS WIRE)--Cadence's Anirudh Devgan to Present at Goldman Sachs Communacopia + Technology Conference.\n\n7 weeks ago - Business Wire\n\n### Cadence Subsystem for PCIe 6.0 Architecture Achieves First-Pass PCI Express Specification Compliance\n\nSAN JOSE, Calif.--(BUSINESS WIRE)---- $CDNS #AIforDesign--Cadence (Nasdaq: CDNS) today announced that its PHY and controller IP for the PCI Express® (PCIe®) 6.0 specification, implemented in the TSMC ...\n\n7 weeks ago - Business Wire\n\n### The Big 3: CDNS, NET, WMT\n\n@ProsperTradingAcademy's Mike Shorr highlight three stocks he sees holding plenty of trading opportunities ahead. He points to Cadence Design Systems (CDNS) gaining momentum, sees Cloudflare (NET) on ...\n\n### Cadence Design Systems Transcript: Deutsche Bank 2026 Technology Conference\n\nThe conference highlighted accelerating industry convergence, AI-driven productivity gains, and robust growth across EDA, SDA, and IP segments. AI super agents and automation are reshaping business models, while strong backlog and recurring revenue provide visibility and resilience.\n\n### Cadence to Present at Deutsche Bank Technology Conference\n\n### Cadence's HypertensionOS Software Announced as Second Participant in FDA's TEMPO to Advance Hypertension Care\n\n### Semiconductor stocks SOAR as strong Microsoft outlook revives AI trade\n\n### Cadence Design price target raised to $400 from $370 at Morgan Stanley","title":"Cadence Design Systems (CDNS) Stock Price & Overview","url":"https://stockanalysis.com/stocks/cdns/"},{"author":null,"id":"https://stockanalysis.com/stocks/cdns/statistics/","image":"https://stockanalysis.com/stockanalysis-1200x630.png","text":"Cadence Design Systems (CDNS) Statistics & Valuation\n\n316.49 +6.84 (2.21%) At close: Oct 23, 2026, 4:00 PM EDT\n\n316.93 +0.44 (0.14%) After-hours: Oct 23, 2026, 7:54 PM EDT\n\n## Total Valuation\n\nCDNS has a market cap or net worth of $87.16 billion. The enterprise value is $88.28 billion.\n\n| Market Cap | 87.16B |\n| --- | --- |\n| Enterprise Value | 88.28B |\n\n## Important Dates\n\nThe next confirmed earnings date is Monday, October 26, 2026, after market close.\n\n| Earnings Date | Oct 26, 2026 |\n| --- | --- |\n| Ex-Dividend Date | n/a |\n\n## Share Statistics\n\nCDNS has 275.39 million shares outstanding. The number of shares has increased by 0.17% in one year.\n\n| Current Share Class | 275.39M |\n| --- | --- |\n| Shares Outstanding | 275.39M |\n| Shares Change (YoY) | +0.17% |\n| Shares Change (QoQ) | +0.89% |\n| Owned by Insiders (%) | 0.34% |\n| Owned by Institutions (%) | 90.30% |\n| Float | 274.17M |\n\n## Valuation Ratios\n\nThe trailing PE ratio is 62.92 and the forward PE ratio is 36.79. CDNS's PEG ratio is 2.44.\n\n| PE Ratio | 62.92 |\n| --- | --- |\n| F